    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n63717" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγ-ιμος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			2.98
		</span></i>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Id.
			6.106
		</span></i>: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέγω</span> B):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>worth mention, notable,
			famous</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλις</span> Il.cc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλισμα, ἔθνος, ἀνήρ</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				1.143
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				171
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				9.64
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. ἐς τὰ πρῶτα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					9.16
				</span></i>
			; -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ώτατος</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				37
			</span></i>; as epith. of temples in Egypt, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱερὸν λ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PTeb.</u>
					302.4
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(i A.D.)</span>, etc. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλλόγιμος</span> is more freq.).</div>
